# S0-CTL (STOP, the control of the window): the window image with EVERY FLAG OFF (the production profile's audited twin with the prefix route's digests on: QWEN_PREFIX_DIGESTS logs slot_sha and logits_sha
# for every prompt, unsalted ones included, the control side of G-NP1 and G-NP2). Tests: the S0 set, concurrent8_skew and the three Lever N exactness shapes.
# READ: admission at 262,144 with NO waiver and NO UNQUALIFIED line; the hashes of concurrent8_steady, concurrent8_code_32k and concurrent8_code_equal EQUAL the production reference, which is the smoke JSON of
# tag v579 (run 37240205944, the production profile on the production base image: the audits change no byte). RECORD every hash, the position-keyed accepted prefixes and the [PREFIX] row digests by tokens_sha.
# STOP RULE: a hash that differs from the reference ends the window (the image is not byte-identical to production with its flags off); no T0 is needed.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W-1 window pack (tp4-w1-levern-jobs: Lever N + prefix reuse, exactness; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/stage1-windows and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order,
# the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the combined branch's engine with the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its
# default); a job that names tp4-serve-10 runs the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box: the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit-digests
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_skew,levern_equal,levern_equal_busy,levern_equal_long
C2_BOX_MINUTES=100
